cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Lixity, please cite it as below."
title: "Lixity — Quantitative text linguistics, stylometry and self-calibrating style references"
version: "1.13.0"
date-released: "2026-09-23"
license: LicenseRef-Lixity-Non-Commercial-License-1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/mfahsold/lixity"
url: "https://mfahsold.github.io/lixity/"
abstract: >-
  Offline, deterministic text-linguistics engine for literary manuscripts:
  sentence rhythm, length-invariant lexical diversity (HD-D, MTLD, MATTR,
  Maas, Yule's K), language-calibrated readability, dialogue share,
  paragraph-accurate tense profiles, and a self-calibrating style reference
  (robust median/MAD bands, significance-adjusted z*, Benjamini-Hochberg /
  Benjamini-Yekutieli FDR, effect sizes) with Structural diagnostics
  (PELT, Mann-Kendall, Sn/Qn, Hill, Wasserstein-KS, Dunning keyness,
  Goh-Barabasi co-occurrence fitness). Pure Python 3.10+, no cloud calls.
authors:
  - family-names: Fahsold
    given-names: Matthias
    email: mfahsold@googlemail.com
keywords:
  - computational linguistics
  - stylometry
  - text analysis
  - literary manuscripts
  - tense profiling
  - style reference
  - lexical diversity
  - readability
  - digital humanities
  - macro-editing
